# R5-4: an index out of range is the implicit `interpreter` throw where the walker already has it -- the ELEM frame of the
# step -- taken by `catch: interpreter ()`.  Natively the access is Q55's (C99, no check): no native row pins it.  The
# methods walked.  Entry 7.
fn: work () int
    []: int a 3
    int: got 1
    ---
        got: a[5]
        got: 2
    ---
    catch: interpreter ()
        got: 7
    return: got
end: work
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: work(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
